<newsitem itemid="588232" id="root" date="1997-05-15" xml:lang="en">
<title>HONG KONG: Prime Success 1996 net up 11.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Prime Success 1996 net up 11.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 22.0     vs 25.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  4.00     vs 4.66</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	nil	vs 14.34 gain</p>
<p>    Net			  118.12   vs 105.71</p>
<p>    Turnover		   1,053.76 vs 1,032.50</p>
<p>    Company name	     Prime Success International Group Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		June 17-20</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 June 27</p>
<p>NOTE - Prime Success is a footwear manufacturer.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one-for-two shares and one 1998 warrant for five shares (after bonus issue of shares). The bonus warrants will be exercisable at any time from June 27, 1997, to June 26, 1998. Each warrant will entitle its holder to subscribe in cash for new shares at an initial subscription price of HK$1.68 per share (subject to adjustments).</p>
<p>Share earnings are based on the weighted average of 531 million shares vs 421 million shares.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 5.5 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 1.5 cents) vs 4.66 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
